   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. The glutaryl linker length (three CH\u2082 between the two C=O groups) is my best reading, because the zigzag bond positions there were hard to resolve.\n\n**Left half**\n- The piperidine nitrogen carries a 4-(trifluoromethoxy)phenylacetyl group.\n- C3 of the piperidine bears F on a hashed bond, and C4 bears O on a wedge. I assigned both centres as R from the drawn geometry.\n- The C4 oxygen links to C2 of a pyridine. This pyridine has a primary carboxamide at C3 and an imidazol-4-yl group at C5.\n\n**Linker**\n- The imidazole N1 connects to a chain of four CH\u2082 groups, then NH, then C(=O)CH\u2082CH\u2082CH\u2082C(=O) (glutaryl), then NH.\n\n**Right half**\n- The NH attaches to a tert-leucine residue, which acylates a 4-hydroxyproline.\n- The proline carboxamide is bound to a 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)benzylamine.\n- I used the standard VHL-ligand stereochemistry: (S)-tert-leucine, and (2S,4R)-hydroxyproline with the OH on a wedge.\n\nI converted each stereo tag to match the atom order in the SMILES string.\n\nSMILES: O=C(Cc1ccc(OC(F)(F)F)cc1)N1CC[C@@H](Oc2ncc(-c3cn(CCCCNC(=O)CCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N4C[C@H](O)C[C@@H]4C(=O)NCc4ccc(cc4)-c4scnc4C)cn3)cc2C(N)=O)[C@H](F)C1"
